<title>USA: PS Colo. confirms Comanche unit outage.</title>
<headline>PS Colo. confirms Comanche unit outage.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public Service Co of Colorado confirmed Thursday the Wednesday outage of a 350 megawatt (MW) unit at the Comanche coal-fired power plant in Pueblo, Colo.</p>
<p>Spokeswoman Susan Stallworth repeated earlier reports that the unit would be out for two to three weeks after an electrical fire in a cable tray.</p>
<p>--D Beasley, Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
